    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Apologies for the abrupt stop! For those US passport holders staying in hotels, you definitely need to secure the appropriate **entry visas** for Vietnam and Thailand, as Singapore is usually quite straightforward for short tourist stays. A crucial thing to check is the **visa-on-arrival (VOA)** process versus needing a pre-arranged e-visa, especially for Vietnam.\n\nTo avoid getting stuck, you must prepare documentation that proves they are legitimate tourists, not intending to work or overstay. This often means having a **confirmed hotel booking** for their entire stay in each city, and critically, **proof of onward travel** (i.e., the flight ticket out of that country to the next destination). Sometimes, border agents look for this proof of leaving within the allotted time frame.\n\nHere is the completed checklist focusing on documentation pitfalls:\n\n1.  **Confirmed Hotel Bookings:** Printouts or digital copies of all hotel reservations for the duration of their stay in Vietnam, Thailand, and Singapore.\n2.  **Proof of Onward Travel:** This is the big one; ensure they have confirmed flight bookings showing they will leave the country before their visa expires.\n3.  **Sufficient Funds:** While not always asked",
